  "brief": "Tradeweb is acquiring Trumid for nearly $2 billion in a deal that will expand its credit capabilities across the entire bond lifecycle.\n\nTradeweb / Trumid (Announced): Tradeweb Acquires Trumid. Tradeweb is acquiring Trumid for nearly $2 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal will expand Tradeweb's credit capabilities across the entire bond lifecycle [4]. Trumid will be acquired in a $1.97 billion cash-and-equity deal [3, 4].\nSilgan / Trivium Packaging (Pending approval): Silgan to Acquire Trivium Packaging. Silgan is acquiring Trivium Packaging for $3.4 billion [5, 6, 7]. Silgan's shares rose 5.5% following the acquisition agreement [11]. The news was reported by multiple financial news outlets [8, 9, 10].\nDream Finders / Beazer Homes (Completed): Dream Finders and Beazer Homes Deal Completed. Dream Finders and Beazer Homes have completed their $2.2 billion all-cash acquisition [13, 14, 15]. The deal marks Dream Finders as the nation's sixth-largest homebuilder [14].\nProofpoint / Varonis (Announced): Proofpoint Acquires Varonis. Proofpoint is acquiring Varonis in a $6.3 billion cash deal [16, 18, 19]. The deal is expected to expand Proofpoint's AI security capabilities [22]. The acquisition is set to be completed in early 2027 [17].\nSalesforce / Braze (Announced): Salesforce to Acquire Braze. Salesforce is acquiring Braze for $5.66 billion in enterprise value [24]. The deal is worth 58% more than Monday's share price [23]. The deal has been announced [24].\nMaximus / Agile Defense (Announced): Maximus to Acquire Agile Defense. Maximus is acquiring Agile Defense for $660M [25, 26]. The deal will advance Maximus' defense and national security growth strategy [26]. No further information is available [26].\nCuraleaf / Aurora (Announced): Curaleaf and Aurora Takeover Bid. Curaleaf is escalating its bid to acquire Aurora, citing an 86% premium and denying diligence issues [27, 28, 29]. Curaleaf has continued to raise its offer to acquire Aurora, with a new bid of $5 per share [28, 30, 32]. Curaleaf has improved its takeover offer for Aurora, with the latest bid being sweetened to $5 per share [31, 33, 34].\nEQT / Cleanaway (Announced): EQT to Acquire Cleanaway. EQT is acquiring Cleanaway in a deal worth A$9.3 billion [35, 36, 40]. Cleanaway has accepted the takeover offer from EQT [40]. The deal was first announced by EQT [35, 36, 37].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- XCF Global Announces Agreement to Acquire Paramount, California Renewable Fuel Production Facility [42].\n- Penske’s go-private deal is about control more than capital [43].\n- Hackensack Meridian Health and Hunterdon Health Sign Definitive Agreement to Merge [44].",
